  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nOnce we get into mid-week, we start seeing the return of (low) rain \nchances. A front stretching all the way up to a low pressure system \nin Maine will start to make its way into the Ohio river valley, \nwhich will increase our rain chances north of I-40. These aren't \ndrought busting rain chances by any means, but enough for some areas \nto see some wetting rain. What's more eye-catching is the cold front \nthat lags behind this moisture and is expected to swing through at \nthe end of the week. This cold front is looking like a real taste of \nfall, dropping our 850mb temperatures by 15 degrees Celsius. At the \nsurface, that translates to highs in the 60s/70s and lows in the 30s \nand 40s for the weekend. Sunday morning, we could see our first \nfrost of the season on the Cumberland Plateau. We will have to keep \nwatching and hope that this time, fall is here to stay.",
